      "properties": {
        "text": "HELM LAB (older template). An idea defined by two IMAGES instead of two prompts.\n\n1) Load image A, run with the name 'imgA' and denoise about 0.55. This records what the model sees in that image.\n2) Load image B, change the name to 'imgB', run again.\n3) Open helm_vector: it combines the two recordings into an axis (A minus B).\nThen use the axis with 'Apply axis'. Same method as the prompt version, but the contrast is visual."
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "HELM LAB (older template). An idea defined by two IMAGES instead of two prompts.\n\n1) Load image A, run with the name 'imgA' and denoise about 0.55. This records what the model sees in that image.\n2) Load image B, change the name to 'imgB', run again.\n3) Open helm_vector: it combines the two recordings into an axis (A minus B).\nThen use the axis with 'Apply axis'. Same method as the prompt version, but the contrast is visual."
      ]
